An array typedef -- `typedef T name[N];`.

micro-c had no form of this. The name was consumed, `[` reached the `;` check,
and the declaration died with "ERROR in typedef statement".

WHAT NEEDED IT. micro-c-libc/setjmp.h has carried a workaround and a note
saying so since it was written:

    NOT `typedef struct {...} jmp_buf[1];`, which is how real libcs write it
    so the name decays to a pointer when passed. micro-c cannot parse a
    typedef of an ARRAY type ... the array typedef is then a real micro-c gap
    rather than a self-inflicted one.

Something needed it. tcc writes

    jmp_buf main_jb;                       tcc.h
    tcc_setjmp(s1, main_jb, ...)           tccrun.c:250

and a plain struct does not decay, so mc-tcc compiling tcc's own source
stopped with "cannot convert 'struct __jmp_buf' to 'void *'".

A POINTER TYPEDEF WOULD ALSO HAVE COMPILED AND WOULD HAVE BEEN WORSE. It makes
`jmp_buf main_jb;` reserve eight bytes rather than 256, so setjmp writes
through an uninitialised pointer -- compiles, links, wrong only at run time,
which is the single failure class this project exists to avoid. Rejected on
those grounds rather than tried and reverted.

THE SIZE IS THE WHOLE IMPLEMENTATION, and that is not a shortcut. micro-c
already treats anything wider than a register as living at an ADDRESS rather
than in one -- the same rule that makes struct arguments, struct assignment and
member access work. So a typedef whose size is N elements wide gets both halves
for free: a declaration reserves N elements, and passing the name yields its
address rather than a load. Nothing else had to change.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. The element type is not recorded, so INDEXING through such
a typedef would stride by the whole array rather than by one element. Nothing
in tcc subscripts one -- jmp_buf is passed and never indexed -- and closing that
would want a case first. Recorded rather than discovered later.

VERIFIED against gcc on both architectures: sizeof(jb) where `typedef long
jb[32]` is 256, a local and a global both reserve it, and passing either to a
`long*` parameter and filling all 32 slots reads back correctly.

    difftest    91 pass / 0 fail amd64, 93 / 0 aarch64, 1 known gap
    the twelve  12 / 12
    tcc unit    micro-c's output is unchanged -- nothing in tcc used an array
                typedef before this, so the feature is additive and inert
                until a header asks for it

